const FAQ_TEXT = "# FAQ (reference answers — keep replies short in chat)\n\n**Q: How much does a new roof / repair cost?**\nA: Honestly, it depends on the size of the roof, the materials, and what shape it's in, so we don't guess over chat. The good news is the estimate is free and there's no obligation. Want me to have someone reach out to set that up?\n\n**Q: How does the free estimate work?**\nA: Someone from our team comes out, takes a look at the roof, explains what they see step by step, and gives you a clear quote. No pressure and no obligation. All I need is your name, number, and the neighborhood or ZIP.\n\n**Q: I have a leak right now / water is coming in. What do I do?**\nA: Sorry you're dealing with that. If water is actively coming in, call us at the office number so we can move fast. If it's safe, put a bucket down and move valuables away from the drip, but please don't go up on the roof yourself. What's the best number to reach you?\n\n**Q: Do you do emergency repairs or tarping?**\nA: Yes, we handle emergency roof repairs. The fastest way to get help is a phone call. [OWNER: VERIFY whether you offer temporary tarping and after-hours/weekend emergency service — the bot will not promise either until you confirm.]\n\n**Q: We had storm / wind damage. Can you help?**\nA: Absolutely. The team can inspect the damage, explain what needs fixing, and document it with photos and an estimate you can use if you file a claim. What's your neighborhood or ZIP?\n\n**Q: Will insurance cover my roof? Can you deal with my insurance?**\nA: Coverage is up to your insurance company, so we can't promise anything there. What we can do is help with documentation, like photos and a detailed estimate, so you have what you need. [OWNER: VERIFY how much claim help you provide.]\n\n**Q: How long does a roof replacement take?**\nA: A lot of our customers mention their roof was done in about a day, but every job is different depending on size, weather, and what we find. The team will give you a realistic timeline with your estimate.\n\n**Q: What warranties do you offer?**\nA: Depending on the system and materials, you can get up to a 50-year manufacturer warranty, and we stand behind our work with a 100% satisfaction guarantee. The team will walk you through the exact warranty for your roof. [OWNER: VERIFY workmanship warranty details if you'd like the bot to mention them.]\n\n**Q: Do you offer financing?**\nA: That's a great question for the team. They can go over payment options with you during the estimate. Want me to have someone call you?  [OWNER: VERIFY — if you offer financing, describe it here (no rates or terms unless you want them quoted).]\n\n**Q: Are you licensed and insured?**\nA: Yes, Alter Phase Roofing is fully licensed and insured. The team is happy to share documentation during your estimate.\n\n**Q: Do you handle permits (NYC DOB)?**\nA: For standard jobs, the team typically takes care of the usual paperwork, and they'll let you know exactly what's needed for your project during the estimate. [OWNER: VERIFY.]\n\n**Q: Do you work on flat roofs?**\nA: Yes, flat roofing is something we do a lot of, for both homes and commercial buildings. The team will recommend the right system after seeing the roof.\n\n**Q: Do you do commercial roofing?**\nA: Yes, we do commercial roof replacements, inspections, flat roofing, and repairs. Is this for a building you own or manage?\n\n**Q: Do you do gutters?**\nA: Yep, we install and repair gutters. Clogged, sagging, or overflowing gutters can cause leaks and damage, so it's smart to get them looked at.\n\n**Q: Do you do siding?**\nA: We do, including siding installation and repair and vinyl siding. Want a free estimate on that?\n\n**Q: Can you fix or install a skylight?**\nA: Yes, we install and repair skylights. Leaky skylights are a really common issue, and usually a fixable one.\n\n**Q: Do you do roof inspections?**\nA: Yes, we do roof inspections for homes and commercial buildings, great if you're buying or selling, or just want peace of mind before winter.\n\n**Q: What areas do you serve?**\nA: We're based in Staten Island and also work in Brooklyn, Manhattan, and around NYC. What neighborhood are you in? [OWNER: VERIFY full service area.]\n\n**Q: Repair or replace — which do I need?**\nA: It really depends on the roof's age and condition. The team will tell you straight if a repair will do the job, and they're known for explaining everything step by step. A free inspection is the best way to find out.\n\n**Q: What should I have ready for the estimate?**\nA: Just the address, a rough idea of the problem (where it leaks, when it started), and any photos you've taken. If you know the roof's age, that helps too.\n\n**Q: Why choose Alter Phase?**\nA: We're the Staten Island roofer a lot of your neighbors already called, with 104 Google reviews. People mention fast replies, professional crews, clean job sites, and fair pricing. Plus we're licensed and insured with a 100% satisfaction guarantee.\n\n**Q: What are your hours? When will someone call me?**\nA: The team will reach out during business hours. If it's an emergency, calling the office directly is always fastest. [OWNER: VERIFY — add your business hours here if you want the bot to share them.]\n\n**Q: Can I just email or text you?**\nA: Of course. You can email info@alterphaseroofing.com, or leave your number here and note that you prefer a text.";
